To me this sounds like it would just add to the tediousness of
Gehennom. Now not only do you need to get through yet some more
levels, but you need to fool around killing more monsters until they
grant intrinsics or items. 

It sounds good in theory, but in practice I just don't see how fishing
for items or intrinsics is going to really make the game more fun.

I personally feel that 3.4 resolved the boringness of gehennom with
the Travel command. 

Honestly if you really want to make gehennom challenging the best way
to do it is simply by unbreaking the combat system in the game. I
don't really know if people -want- to fix gehennom, but thsi is really
the only way to do it if they do. 

The combat system in nethack is broken at high levels. Players have
-30 or better armor class and I don't seem to recall the toughest
monsters in the game having even -10, and there are few monsters with
combat modifiers that can even hope to hit someone with -40 AC.

I think the most obvious method of stripping away some of the
brokenness is to simply make things less practically enchantable by a
factor of +2 or so and giving AC a hard cap of -20 or -25.

This leaves your player far far better off than the monsters but opens
up the possibility that you might get hit once and awhile. 

Ideas to make Gehennom more fun are fine but they won't make it more
challenging unless they do something to the combat system for high
values. 



